# State this app writes, not source it ships.
#
# `AUTH=builtin` keeps its users here — the sqlite file named in
# lumenjs.config.ts, plus the `-wal` and `-shm` files SQLite's WAL mode keeps
# beside it. It holds password hashes and live session state, so it is the one
# directory in this package that must never reach a commit; a repository is not
# a place a credential can be taken back out of.
#
# The root .gitignore already covers node_modules, dist and test-results. This
# file exists for what phase 4 added.
/data/

# Where the local storage adapter puts uploads when no S3 bucket is configured.
/uploads/

# `lumenjs build` output: the client bundle, the server bundle and the route
# manifest. The Dockerfile builds it inside the image and .dockerignore keeps
# any host copy out of the context, so a checked-in one could only ever be a
# stale second answer.
/.lumenjs/

# `lumenjs build` writes this three-line SSR entry into the project root, adds
# it to the Rollup inputs, and deletes it in a `finally`. A build that is
# interrupted — Ctrl-C, a killed container, a failure in a parallel target —
# never reaches the finally, so the file is left behind at the top of the
# package looking like source. It is not; it is regenerated on every build.
/__nk_ssr_entry.js
.console-dev.log
